# Duet firmware files that a separately published build replaces.
#
# One line per file:
#
#   <file> sha256:<checksum of the published build> <https location>
#
# The file has to be one the reprapfirmware package delivers below
# /opt/dsf/sd/firmware, because that is the name RepRapFirmware derives from
# the board type when it flashes; a build under any other name is never used.
# Only a published build is taken, checked against the pin: no local path, no
# fallback, a mismatch stops the build. See "Replacing a Duet firmware file"
# in the README, in particular why the build needs a version string of its
# own before any board is flashed with it.
#
# Example:
#   Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:0123...cdef https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/v3.7.0-rc.1+mp1/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin sha256:5b750b2f57d8bfeb55630d62f91cd18c93edca34c21ea3cd0244ffacaa1b7ed3 https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.6/Duet3Firmware_TOOL1LC.bin
Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin sha256:fa95b85a2a03779a97ec208b98921e3aed9a775ef8fa60d7523e2fd9b7a31800 https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.6/Duet3Firmware_EXP1HCL.bin
Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin sha256:cf379a37c8cb5f0a8d9286d35f7d0f7751bbe5c4039c5e7cd9b2fba06b3ed697 https://github.com/Meltingplot/Duet3Expansion/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.6/Duet3Firmware_SZP.bin
# Mainboard: RepRapFirmware 3.7-dev at upstream 3.7.0-rc.1+3 (3f6ada0), built
# by us against the Meltingplot library forks with a version string of its
# own, so DuetControlServer flashes it on an image update.
Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin sha256:5e0a8fff28c915141a177fd1a478fff666bd40868cea5f76ae6930ff40acf5da https://github.com/Meltingplot/RepRapFirmware/releases/download/3.7.0-rc.1%2B3-mp.5/Duet3Firmware_MB6HC.bin
